// An empty path names no file, so open in mode "r" raises the runtime error its
// section gives for a file it cannot open (spec/05-stdlib.md, Strings the host
// reads). A consumer that resolves the empty path to the working directory opens
// that directory in mode "r" and goes on.
// STATUS: error
// CHECK: before
// COVERS: host-string open
print "before";
open("", "r");
